    "teacher_markdown": "## **Teacher Tips**\r\n\r\n### **Students may assume AI's guesses are equally reliable in both datasets**\r\n\r\nStudents may see that AI can still fill in the missing values and assume its answers are just as trustworthy as they were with labeled fields. Encourage them to compare the amount of context available by asking: **\"What information did the field labels give AI in the previous level that it doesn't have now?\"**\r\n\r\nRelevant comparison:\r\n```markdown\r\nLabeled: teamCode, checkInBlock, pointsEarned\r\nMystery: unclear or unlabeled fields\r\n```\r\n\r\nReinforce that less context can make AI's guesses less grounded and more uncertain.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### **Students may focus only on whether AI filled every blank**\r\n\r\nSome students may judge the response as successful simply because every missing value was replaced. Encourage them to evaluate the reasoning by asking: **\"What evidence does AI have that this value belongs here?\"**\r\n\r\nA filled-in value can look reasonable without actually being supported by the data. Students should distinguish between **completing the dataset** and **accurately recovering missing information**.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### **Students may not connect labels to meaning**\r\n\r\nStudents may notice that the datasets look different without recognizing why labels matter. Ask: **\"If you see a value like `18`, how does knowing the field is called `pointsEarned` change your interpretation of that number?\"**\r\n\r\nRelevant idea:\r\n```markdown\r\nValue + clear label → more context\r\nValue without a clear label → more possible interpretations\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis helps students recognize that meaningful labels provide context that both people and AI can use when interpreting data.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### **Students may use the same prompt and expect the same quality of response**\r\n\r\nBecause the instructions suggest using a similar prompt, this is a useful opportunity to discuss how the **same prompt can produce less reliable results when the available context changes**.\r\n\r\nAsk: **\"Did your prompt get worse, or did the AI have less information to work with?\"**\r\n\r\nThis reinforces that AI output depends not only on how a prompt is written, but also on the quality and context of the data provided."
  },
